rules_version = '2';

// Firestore security rules for Tutorly. Owner: Member 1 (Week 3).
//
// This file is LOCKED on purpose: it allows nothing. If someone publishes it as
// it is, the app cannot read or write any data, which is safe but useless. That
// is better than a file that is open by accident.
//
// During Weeks 1 and 2 the team builds in the console's "test mode", which
// allows everything for a limited time. Before submission, replace the lines
// below with real rules and publish them (Firebase console > Firestore Database
// > Rules). Test every rule in the Rules Playground in the same page.
//
// What the real rules must do (see docs/FIRESTORE_SCHEMA.md for the fields):
//   users/{uid}           the owner reads and edits their own document, but can
//                         never change `role`. Nobody can create a user with
//                         role 'admin' from the app. Admins can read all.
//   tutors/{uid}          the owner edits their own profile but not
//                         `verificationStatus`. Logged-in students read tutors
//                         whose verificationStatus is 'approved'. Only admins
//                         change verification fields.
//   bookings/{id}         only the student and the tutor of that booking read
//                         it; only the student creates it; only the tutor
//                         accepts or rejects it. Admins can read all.
//   conversations/{id}    only the two people in `participantIds`, and the same
//   and messages          for the messages inside.
//   notifications/{id}    a user reads and marks as read only their own.
//   everything else       denied.
//
// A rule can read another document with get(), for example to find the caller's
// role in users/{request.auth.uid}. Docs: https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/security/get-started
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
